@cindex Benchmarking

When you need to compare the performance of different implementations or tools, @uref{https://github.com/sharkdp/hyperfine,hyperfine} is excellent for benchmarking command-line programs:

@example
$ hyperfine --warmup 3 'fd -e jpg' 'find . -iname "*.jpg"'
Benchmark #1: fd -e jpg
  Time (mean ± σ):      51.4 ms ±   2.9 ms    [User: 121.0 ms, System: 160.5 ms]
  Range (min … max):    44.2 ms …  60.1 ms    56 runs

Benchmark #2: find . -iname "*.jpg"
  Time (mean ± σ):      1.126 s ±  0.101 s    [User: 141.1 ms, System: 956.1 ms]
  Range (min … max):    0.975 s …  1.287 s    10 runs

Summary
  'fd -e jpg' ran
   21.89 ± 2.33 times faster than 'find . -iname "*.jpg"'
@end example

@quotation
For web development, browser developer tools include excellent profilers. See the @uref{https://profiler.firefox.com/docs/,Firefox Profiler} and @uref{https://developers.google.com/web/tools/chrome-devtools/rendering-tools,Chrome DevTools} documentation.
