@code{git restore}: discard changes
@end itemize

@node Git - Advanced Git, Git - Miscellaneous, Git - Git command-line interface, Git
@unnumberedsec Advanced Git
@cindex Advanced Git

@itemize
@item
@code{git config}: Git is @uref{https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config,highly customizable}
@item
@code{git clone --depth=1}: shallow clone, without entire version history
@item
@code{git add -p}: interactive staging
@item
@code{git rebase -i}: interactive rebasing
@item
@code{git blame}: show who last edited which line
@item
@code{git stash}: temporarily remove modifications to working directory
@item
@code{git bisect}: binary search history (e.g. for regressions)
@item
@code{git revert}: create a new commit that reverses the effect of an earlier commit
@item
@code{git worktree}: check out multiple branches at the same time
@item
@code{.gitignore}: @uref{https://git-scm.com/docs/gitignore,specify} intentionally untracked files to ignore
@end itemize

@node Git - Miscellaneous, Git - Resources, Git - Advanced Git, Git
@unnumberedsec Miscellaneous
@cindex Miscellaneous

@itemize
@item
@strong{GUIs}: there are many @uref{https://git-scm.com/downloads/guis,GUI clients} out there for Git. We personally don't use them and use the command-line interface instead.
@item
@strong{Shell integration}: it's super handy to have a Git status as part of your shell prompt (@uref{https://github.com/olivierverdier/zsh-git-prompt,zsh}, @uref{https://github.com/magicmonty/bash-git-prompt,bash}). Often included in frameworks like @uref{https://github.com/ohmyzsh/ohmyzsh,Oh My Zsh}.
@item
@strong{Editor integration}: similarly to the above, handy integrations with many features. @uref{https://github.com/tpope/vim-fugitive,fugitive.vim} is the standard one for Vim.
@item
@strong{Workflows}: we taught you the data model, plus some basic commands; we didn't tell you what practices to follow when working on big projects (and there are @uref{https://nvie.com/posts/a-successful-git-branching-model/,many} @uref{https://www.endoflineblog.com/gitflow-considered-harmful,different} @uref{https://www.atlassian.com/git/tutorials/comparing-workflows/gitflow-workflow,approaches}).
@item
@strong{GitHub}: Git is not GitHub. GitHub has a specific way of contributing code to other projects, called @uref{https://help.github.com/en/github/collaborating-with-issues-and-pull-requests/about-pull-requests,pull requests}.
@item
@strong{Other Git providers}: GitHub is not special: there are many Git repository hosts, like @uref{https://about.gitlab.com/,GitLab} and @uref{https://bitbucket.org/,BitBucket}.
@end itemize

